 compilation and both actual IPA/source/relink/notice/kit gates passed once.307 notice packages,0gaps.\n\nCurrent complete source78,336,612bytes SHA2561ba83e045df171a3ca51bc7b1b44aaec131f6489e07d73778b6fafeb917e95cf. Native kit35,149,949bytes SHA256e814dd588ff46be402d0372e2f66ce2154f5e3661a3ded93224bb0f1bfe41bf6. Transfer-only40778539399 verified all9server asset hashes/sizes and2 preserved owned fixture IDs. The draft stays private/unpublished, release_ready=false; matching source accompanies the binary candidates.\n\nTin reported Mac signing/export/install and manual launch of the previous8eaf app, then a sign-in/unlock crash. This source defect is fixed/tested, but physical crash resolution is not yet established. Use app-installer/device/UPDATE-EXISTING-KIT.md to merge the pinned new kit while retaining existing local private signing products and forcing the new Rust library to relink, then update the same installed identity. Do not uninstall the app or upload user signed IPAs, profiles, keys, account data or pairing exports.\n\nExisting routine MacBook/USB phone/network/kit/trusted-dependency approval persists; significantly larger Xcode installations and Apple-credential changes need separate approval. Direct chat computer control remains unavailable; manual guided setup is active. Broader capability limits and foreground-unlock/expiry-recovery constraints remain explicit. App Installer stays this chat’s task; Unit Creator/Offline have their own chat.\n"}